# Operating system commands: window title and its stack, hyperlinks (OSC 8).

test OSC 0 sets the window title
spec xterm ctlseqs OSC 0: change icon name and window title
size 10 4
feed \e]0;hello\a
title hello
screen
||

test OSC 2 sets the window title
spec xterm ctlseqs OSC 2: change window title
size 10 4
feed \e]2;world\a
title world

test OSC 2 ended by ST
spec xterm ctlseqs: xterm accepts either BEL or ST for terminating OSC
size 10 4
feed \e]2;world\e\\
title world

test OSC 1 changes the icon name, not the window title
spec xterm ctlseqs OSC 1: change icon name
size 10 4
feed \e]2;window\a\e]1;icon\a
title window

test a title may hold any text
spec xterm ctlseqs OSC Ps ; Pt
size 10 4
feed \e]2;日本 語 ü\a
title 日本 語 ü

test the last title wins
spec xterm ctlseqs OSC 2
size 10 4
feed \e]2;one\a\e]2;two\a
title two

test a title does not appear on the screen
spec ECMA-48 8.3.89 OSC: the string is a command string, not text
size 10 4
feed a\e]2;hidden\ab
screen
|ab|

test a title can be pushed and popped
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI 2 2 ; 0 t saves the title on a stack, CSI 2 3 ; 0 t restores it
size 10 4
feed \e]2;first\a\e[22;0t\e]2;second\a
title second
feed \e[23;0t
title first

test the title stack holds several titles
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI 2 2 ; 0 t, CSI 2 3 ; 0 t: a stack
size 10 4
feed \e]2;a\a\e[22;0t\e]2;b\a\e[22;0t\e]2;c\a\e[23;0t
title b
feed \e[23;0t
title a

test a window title push and pop works with Ps = 2
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI 2 2 ; 2 t and CSI 2 3 ; 2 t: window title
size 10 4
feed \e]2;one\a\e[22;2t\e]2;two\a\e[23;2t
title one

test OSC 8 makes the following cells a link
spec OSC 8 hyperlinks: all subsequent cells that are painted are hyperlinks to this target
size 20 4
feed \e]8;;http://example.com\aLINK\e]8;;\a plain
cell 1,1 text=L link=http://example.com
cell 1,4 text=K link=http://example.com
cell 1,5 text=\s link=none
cell 1,6 text=p link=none
screen
|LINK plain|

test OSC 8 ended by ST
spec OSC 8 hyperlinks: the sequence is terminated with ST, BEL is used as well
size 20 4
feed \e]8;;http://example.com\e\\LINK\e]8;;\e\\x
cell 1,1 link=http://example.com
cell 1,4 link=http://example.com
cell 1,5 text=x link=none

test OSC 8 with an id
spec OSC 8 hyperlinks: params is a list of key=value assignments separated by colons, the id key is defined
size 20 4
feed \e]8;id=a1:foo=bar;https://example.org/x\aA\e]8;;\a
cell 1,1 text=A link=https://example.org/x

test switching links without closing the first
spec OSC 8 hyperlinks: it is perfectly legal to switch from one hyperlink to another without explicitly closing the first one
size 20 4
feed \e]8;;http://one.example\aA\e]8;;http://two.example\aB\e]8;;\a
cell 1,1 text=A link=http://one.example
cell 1,2 text=B link=http://two.example

test closing a link that is not open is harmless
spec OSC 8 hyperlinks: it is perfectly legal to close a hyperlink when it's not actually open
size 20 4
feed \e]8;;\ax
cell 1,1 text=x link=none

test a link goes on across a line break
spec OSC 8 hyperlinks: the hyperlink is a cell attribute like color
size 20 4
feed \e]8;;http://example.com\aab\r\ncd\e]8;;\a
cell 1,2 link=http://example.com
cell 2,1 text=c link=http://example.com
cell 2,2 text=d link=http://example.com

test a link goes on across a wrap
spec OSC 8 hyperlinks: the hyperlink is a cell attribute like color
size 4 4
feed \e]8;;http://example.com\aabcdef
cell 2,1 text=e link=http://example.com

test spaces inside a link are part of it
spec OSC 8 hyperlinks: all subsequent cells that are painted
size 20 4
feed \e]8;;http://example.com\aa\sb\e]8;;\a
cell 1,2 text=\s link=http://example.com

test a link and a color are independent
spec OSC 8 hyperlinks: you can think of the hyperlink as yet another attribute
size 20 4
feed \e]8;;http://example.com\a\e[31mA\e[0mB\e]8;;\a
cell 1,1 text=A fg=idx:1 link=http://example.com
cell 1,2 text=B fg=default link=http://example.com

test SGR 0 does not end a link
spec OSC 8 hyperlinks: an OSC 8 just changes the hyperlink; SGR is another attribute
size 20 4
feed \e]8;;http://example.com\a\e[1mA\e[0mB
cell 1,2 text=B attrs=none link=http://example.com

test an untouched cell has no link
spec OSC 8 hyperlinks: only painted cells are links
size 20 4
feed \e]8;;http://example.com\aA
cell 1,5 text=\s link=none

test text before the link is not part of it
spec OSC 8 hyperlinks: all subsequent cells
size 20 4
feed ab\e]8;;http://example.com\acd
cell 1,2 text=b link=none
cell 1,3 text=c link=http://example.com

test a link target may contain a semicolon
convention the target is everything after the second separator
size 20 4
feed \e]8;;http://example.com/a;b\aX
cell 1,1 text=X link=http://example.com/a;b

test an empty title is no title
convention xterm shows its default title again when a program sets an empty one
known-fail: alacritty – the title becomes the empty string
size 10 4
feed \e]2;x\a\e]2;\a
title none

test the colors a program sets are kept until it resets them, and a query answers them
spec xterm ctlseqs: OSC 4 sets a palette entry, OSC 10 the foreground, OSC 104 and OSC 110 reset them
size 10 4
feed \e]4;1;rgb:12/34/56\a\e]4;1;?\a\e]10;#fff\a\e]10;?\a
reply \e]4;1;rgb:1212/3434/5656\a\e]10;rgb:f0f0/f0f0/f0f0\a
feed \e]104;1\a\e]110\a\e]4;1;?\a
reply~ \e]4;1;rgb:*/*/*\a

test a spec with # is the top bits of the byte and rgb: is scaled
spec X(7) color strings: #rgb is the most significant bits (#3a7 is #3000a0007000), rgb:r/g/b is scaled so that f, ff, fff and ffff are all full
size 10 4
feed \e]4;1;#f00\a\e]4;1;?\a\e]4;2;rgb:f/8/0\a\e]4;2;?\a\e]4;3;#abcdef012345\a\e]4;3;?\a
reply \e]4;1;rgb:f0f0/0000/0000\a\e]4;2;rgb:ffff/8888/0000\a\e]4;3;rgb:abab/efef/2323\a

test the special colors are OSC 4 from 256 and OSC 5
spec xterm ctlseqs: OSC 5 sets the special colors (bold, underline, blink, reverse, italic), OSC 4 names them from 256, OSC 105 resets them
known-fail: alacritty – no special colors (OSC 5) and no OSC 13 to 19
size 10 4
feed \e]5;1;#112233\a\e]5;1;?\a\e]4;257;?\a\e]4;256;#445566\a\e]5;0;?\a
reply \e]5;1;rgb:1111/2222/3333\a\e]4;257;rgb:1111/2222/3333\a\e]5;0;rgb:4444/5555/6666\a
feed \e]105;0\a\e]5;0;?\a\e]5;1;?\a
reply~ \e]5;0;rgb:*/*/*\a\e]5;1;rgb:1111/2222/3333\a
feed \e]105\a\e]5;1;?\a
reply~ \e]5;1;rgb:*/*/*\a
feed \e]5;9;?\a
reply none

test OSC 10 sets the colors after it too, and OSC 110 to 119 reset them one by one
spec xterm ctlseqs: OSC 10 ; Pt ; Pt sets the foreground and the background; OSC 110 to 119 reset the dynamic colors 10 to 19
known-fail: alacritty – no special colors (OSC 5) and no OSC 13 to 19
size 10 4
feed \e]10;#101010;#202020;#303030\a\e]10;?\a\e]11;?\a\e]12;?\a
reply \e]10;rgb:1010/1010/1010\a\e]11;rgb:2020/2020/2020\a\e]12;rgb:3030/3030/3030\a
feed \e]111\a\e]13;#404040\a\e]13;?\a\e]113\a\e]10;?\a
reply \e]13;rgb:4040/4040/4040\a\e]10;rgb:1010/1010/1010\a

test a full reset puts the colors back
spec xterm ctlseqs: RIS resets the colors a program set
size 10 4
feed \e]4;5;#123456\a\e]5;2;#123456\a\e]11;#654321\a\ec\e]4;5;?\a\e]11;?\a
reply~ \e]4;5;rgb:*/*/*\a\e]11;rgb:*/*/*\a
